course: dictionary
lesson: 5287
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer means. The word jumper is a good example. In «Grandma knits you a jumper you do not like», the clues are knits and you put it on, so a jumper is a warm knitted top with long sleeves.
explain: Now look at the words around it. In «The long jumper flew over the sandpit», the clues are long, flew and sandpit, so this jumper is a person who jumps, like a long jumper in athletics. The spelling is the same, but the meaning is different. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Places can change a meaning too. In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, a jumper is a top you pull over your head. In the US it means a sleeveless dress worn over a blouse, which the UK calls a pinafore. When you are not sure, check the other clues, and then a dictionary can settle it.
fact: A jumper can be a warm knitted top with long sleeves.
fact: A jumper can also be a person or animal that jumps, like a high jumper.
fact: In the US, a jumper is a sleeveless dress worn over a blouse.
fact: A school jumper is part of the uniform, often with the school logo.
fact: Other phrases with jumper include «woolly jumper», «Christmas jumper» and «long jumper».
exercise: «The cold wind blew, so Ayesha pulled on her woolly jumper.» What is a jumper here? | A sleeveless dress worn over a blouse | *A warm knitted top with long sleeves | A person who leaps over a bar
exercise: «Sam was the best long jumper on sports day.» What kind of jumper is Sam? | *A person who jumps in athletics | A sleeveless dress worn over a blouse | A warm knitted top
exercise: In the US, what does jumper mean? | A high jump bar | A bouncy toy on a spring | *A sleeveless dress worn over a blouse | A knitted top with long sleeves
test: «Mum saw the crumbs on his jumper, and he still said no.» Where are the crumbs? | *On his warm top | On the high jump bar | On the sandpit | On the school logo sign
test: Which phrase names an item of school uniform? | High jumper | Long jumper | *School jumper | Christmas jumper
exam: Which phrase uses jumper to mean a person who jumps? | Woolly jumper | *High jumper | Christmas jumper | School jumper
